                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "229321021",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198087791730",
                            "num_reviews": 31,
                            "playtime_forever": 237,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 112,
                            "last_played": 1789164070
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Having never played the original I was curious as to what to expect when I got this game. After having played it for around two hours I can see where the inspiration for Metroid Fusion came from! They straight up just copied this game's map structure and big antagonist. The game is so good though and felt difficult, but fair. I'd die but even dying while exploring a new area didn't really feel like a setback because of the chip system. I will say I think it's a bit simplistic sometimes but I do really enjoy the gameplay and atmosphere. The remake's art direction is on point and I love their sprite work and new enemy designs. I also had the pleasure of meeting the creator at a gaming convention and the guy seemed VERY nice and I had a great time talking to him.\r\n\r\nThe game got it's DNA carbon copied by nintendo, so you know it's good.",
